    "updated_at": "2018-11-02T10:13:04Z",
    "body": "@MattMenke2 right, Chrome now fails the `,bb-8` test (it doesn't result in exposure of the `bb-8` header, whereas before it would likely have exposed `bb-8` as is required behavior for this header. So that's a regression of sorts in a way.\r\n\r\n(Still looking for thoughts on ABNF versus fully-defined parsers. I'm somewhat inclined to go with the latter, but I'll do some more research.)",
